<title>POLAND: BRE plunges after revising '96 net down.</title>
<headline>BRE plunges after revising '96 net down.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's Bank Rozwoju Eksportu SA (BRE) plunged 9.9 percent to 77 zlotys after Wednesday's news the bank revised down its 1996 net profit to 114.7 million zlotys from 134.9 million zlotys, traders said.</p>
<p>Turnover was at 5.5 million zlotys.</p>
<p>Traders said the stock's balanced trade after price-fixing signalled a slower fall if not a rebound on Thursday.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
